aftermath is a new expansion coming to  Mortal Kombat 11 and it adds new  characters story content and more here's  what you need to know yes you heard  right new story content is coming to MK  11 it's the first time a Mortal Kombat  game has gotten an expansion like this  which adds a new epilogue focusing on  fire god Liu Kang as he attempts to  create a new timeline after the events  of MK 11 he'll see some familiar faces  along the way including Shang Tsung who  was absent in the main story and added  later as a DLC fighter other characters  include the wind-god Fujian and a  four-armed half human half Dragon Shiva  who both joined the roster as playable  characters the third new fighter is none  other than Robocop and yes he will be  voiced by original actor Peter Weller so  you've got new characters joining the  fight but there are also some new stages  to fight in they're coming alongside  aftermath as a free update for all  players stages include the classic  Deadpool from mk2 and the soul chamber  from MK 3 complete with brutal stage  fatalities the update also includes the  return of friendships which are like  fatalities but not so mean your opponent  still suffers a nasty defeat but at  least the matches end on a lighter note  friendships new stages and stage  fatalities will be available to all MK  11 players you don't have to buy  aftermath to get them if you are looking  to purchase the expansion you have a few  options if you already own MK 11 the  aftermath upgrade will cost you 40 bucks  you can also get that bundled with the  previously released combat pack which  includes the six current DLC characters  450 if you don't own MK 11 you can get  the aftermath collection for 60 bucks  that includes the base game combat pack  and the aftermath expansion you'll  actually be able to jump right into the  game though you will have to wait for  the aftermath content like everyone else  the expansion launches on May 26th and  it's coming to ps4 Xbox one PC switch  and stadia stay tuned a game spot for a  closer look at the new characters headed  your way  [Music]  you
 

